__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Raw model event streams from run_evals.py. Regenerable by re-running a sweep,
# ~4MB, and they exist only to derive trigger rate. Verdicts and reviews are the
# evidence and are committed; the streams are not.
evals/**/events.jsonl
# The grader's raw event stream, same reasoning as the reviewer's above: a transcript
# of a run, regenerable, and it carries the staged workspace path. Found by the
# portable-evidence rule the moment a run wrote one -- a new evidence file that no
# ignore rule covered is a leak waiting for the next commit.
evals/**/judge_stream.jsonl
# Research reports stay out of version control. The gap register does not, and the
# distinction is the point: an adoption lands only when it closes a *named, cited* gap,
# so the register is the citation list for that test. Ignored, it made every "closes G7"
# claim in this history cite a row that existed on one machine and in no clone -- the test
# unverifiable by construction while appearing to be enforced.
#
# `/docs/*`, not `/docs`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent *directory* is
# excluded, so the negation below was silently inert until the pattern excluded the
# contents rather than the directory. The rule looked right and did nothing.
/docs/*
!/docs/named-gaps.md

# Scratch directory for probes and temporary run artifacts. Lives inside the tree so a
# staged path never carries a per-user temporary directory, and ignored so nothing in it is
# ever published. Never a place to keep evidence.
/probe
# The grader raw reply, same reasoning as its event stream above.
evals/**/judge_reply.txt
